drm: add a KMS driver for the H713 AFBD scanout engine

This gives the projector a DRM card node, so any DRM client -- mpv
--vo=drm, a compositor, fbcon -- can present on the panel. Until now the
only way to put a frame on screen was a tool that mapped 0x05600000
through /dev/mem and poked the AFBD registers itself, which meant every
program that wanted the display had to reimplement the commit sequence and
no two could share it. (It comes up as card1 in practice: panfrost takes
minor 0 as a render-only device.)

The driver adopts a display that is ALREADY RUNNING and deliberately keeps
its hands off everything else. On this board the panel is brought up
before Linux: U-Boot's h713_disp loads the MIPS co-processor, which
programs the VBlender timing and the LVDS PHY. Nothing in Linux can do
that bring-up yet, so this driver never touches timing, the PHY, or
rst_bus_disp -- asserting that reset would kill a panel it cannot bring
back. It owns exactly two things: which buffer is scanned out, and when
the swap happens. Geometry is read back out of the AFBD registers rather
than hardcoded, and probe fails with a pointed message if it reads zero,
which is what "you booted without h713_disp" looks like.

The commit sequence is not new work and not guessed. It is the one
tools/video/gles-play.c uses, which sustained 59.71 fps over 2700 frames
at a measured 0.00% tearing rate against a 16.94% positive control:

	write SRC = buffer address; clear STATUS; set CTRL bit 0; READY = 1

The one thing dropped from it is gles-play's 50 ms poll of STATUS bit 1.
READY latches at the next vsync, so the flip completes on the vblank
interrupt and the page-flip event is armed against it -- no spinning in an
atomic path, and clients get a present timestamp that corresponds to an
actual present.

The vsync interrupt protocol (status and enable bytes at +0xc0 and +0xc4,
write-1-to-clear) comes from the vendor DECD driver's dec_vsync_handler().
That is inherited RE and this project has been burned by inherited claims,
but this one carries hardware evidence: an out-of-bounds write in that
handler crashed the board every ~100 vsyncs, i.e. every ~1.7 s, which only
happens if the interrupt genuinely fires at 60 Hz.

Framebuffers come from the system CMA pool. A dedicated memory-region is
supported but optional, and not used by default, because a dma-coherent
reserved pool allocates in power-of-two page orders: a 3.6 MiB framebuffer
occupies a 4 MiB slot, so a 16 MiB pool yields exactly four. That is not a
theoretical limit -- it was measured. With the fbdev console holding one,
a client can get three, and mpv wants more: it dies at CREATE_DUMB with
ENOMEM. CMA allocates by range, neither rounding up nor imposing that
ceiling, and cma=128M on this board leaves room for cedrus as well.

HARDWARE-VERIFIED on the bench board (2026-08-15): probe reads back
"adopting 1280x720, stride 5120, source 6c100000"; 1320 page flips across
three runs complete at 59.71 fps -- the panel's exact rate -- with zero
timeouts; sampling AFBD's source register during a run shows it
alternating between two client buffers, so scanout really is being
reprogrammed; and 2254 interrupts on GICv2 142 confirm the vblank bits
inherited from DECD are right. Operator-confirmed as a Linux login prompt
on the projector.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/Kconfig
@@ -98,6 +98,25 @@
 
 	  If M is selected, the module will be built as pixpaper.ko.
 
+config DRM_SUN50I_H713_AFBD
+	tristate "DRM support for the Allwinner H713 AFBD scanout engine"
+	depends on DRM && (ARCH_SUNXI || COMPILE_TEST)
+	depends on OF
+	select DRM_CLIENT_SELECTION
+	select DRM_GEM_DMA_HELPER
+	select DRM_KMS_HELPER
+	help
+	  KMS driver for the AFBD scanout engine on the Allwinner H713, as
+	  used in HY200-class projectors.
+
+	  It adopts a display that firmware has already brought up -- the MIPS
+	  co-processor programs the panel timing and LVDS PHY before Linux
+	  starts -- and drives only buffer selection and page flips, so any
+	  DRM client can present on the panel. It never touches timing or the
+	  display reset.
+
+	  If M is selected the module will be called sun50i-h713-afbd.
+
 config TINYDRM_HX8357D
 	tristate "DRM support for HX8357D display panels"
 	depends on DRM && SPI
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/Makefile
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_GM12U320)		+= gm12u320.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_MIPI_DBI)	+= panel-mipi-dbi.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_PIXPAPER)              += pixpaper.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_SUN50I_H713_AFBD)	+= sun50i-h713-afbd.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_TINYDRM_HX8357D)		+= hx8357d.o
